NetworkResourceLoader: a cached redirect continues with this load's request, not the stored one

Applies to WebKitGTK and WPE WebKit 2.54.1 (patch -p1); already part of
leopard-darwin9-wpe-2.54.1-full.patch, so ./build.sh fetch does not apply this file.

A disk-cached redirect was replayed with the request stored in the cache entry. The entry's key
has no requester or destination, so the stored request can come from another kind of load of
the same URL: youtube.com's page fetch()es https://youtube.com/, and its 301 replaces the one
the navigation stored. The next navigation to youtube.com then continued as that fetch
(requester Fetch, Sec-Fetch-Mode: cors, its cache headers and first party). YouTube's service
worker took the navigation as a subresource (no ContinueDidReceiveResponse), and the COOP
browsing-context-group switch resumed the parked loader in the new process with an empty
ResourceResponse: a blank page, or an empty download in browsers that download unsupported types.
Build the redirected request from the current request, as a network redirect does, and take
only the destination URL from the cache.

diff -ruN --no-dereference -x __pycache__ a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp
--- a/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/NetworkProcess/NetworkResourceLoader.cpp
@@ -1912,7 +1912,16 @@
     LOG(NetworkCache, "(NetworkProcess) Executing cached redirect");
 
     m_isWaitingContinueWillSendRequestForCachedRedirect = true;
-    willSendRedirectedRequest(WTF::move(request), ResourceRequest { *entry->redirectRequest() }, ResourceResponse { entry->response() }, [](auto) { });
+    // Build the redirected request from this load's request, as a network redirect does; only the
+    // destination comes from the cache. The cache key has no requester or destination, so the stored
+    // request may belong to another kind of load of the same URL (youtube.com's page fetch()es
+    // https://youtube.com/, which replaces the navigation's cached 301). Replaying it verbatim turned
+    // the next navigation into that fetch (requester Fetch, its Sec-Fetch-* and cache headers, its
+    // first party): a service worker then skipped ContinueDidReceiveResponse, and a COOP process swap
+    // gave the new process an empty response.
+    auto redirectRequest = request.redirectedRequest(entry->response(), parameters().shouldClearReferrerOnHTTPSToHTTPRedirect);
+    redirectRequest.setURL(URL { entry->redirectRequest()->url() });
+    willSendRedirectedRequest(WTF::move(request), WTF::move(redirectRequest), ResourceResponse { entry->response() }, [](auto) { });
 }
 
 IPC::Connection* NetworkResourceLoader::messageSenderConnection() const
